From 11557175471b03d72e3b0d74ccee19a75b6c3cf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayneelatintel <jayneel.vora@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:07:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] Vulkan: Q2_K/Q3_K decode matvec for Intel Xe2/Xe3 iGPUs

On these iGPUs the generic q8_1 matvec (mul_mat_vecq.comp) is limited
by instruction issue, not memory: with the weights in cache it is no
faster. mul_mat_vecq_xe.comp replaces it for Q2_K and Q3_K, n = 1..8,
plain and MUL_MAT_ID (fused bias/scale kept through reduce_result):

- one 16-lane subgroup per workgroup, 4 lanes per row; a lane owns the
  four scale groups that share one set of quant dwords (and Q3_K hmask
  dwords), so it loads them once per block and the plane masks are
  constants
- fields masked in place and dotted with the mixed-sign dot product,
  the power of two removed once per group
- Q3_K's 2-byte-aligned blocks read as aligned dwords, realigned only
  when needed; rows assigned so that branch stays uniform
- activations, their per-group sums and scales prepared once per block
  for all rows of the workgroup

On by default on the Intel devices ggml-vulkan classifies as Xe2 that
have integer dot products and 16-lane subgroups. GGML_VK_XE_MMVQ=0
turns it off; GGML_VK_XE_MMVQ_ROWS sets the rows per workgroup (a
multiple of 4, default 8); GGML_VK_XE_MODE selects diagnostics (1 loads
only, 2 weights in cache; wrong results). Also GGML_VK_RM_KQ,
GGML_VK_RM_KQ_INT and GGML_VK_DMMV_WG override the stock matvec's rows
and workgroup size.

test-backend-ops: eval cases at the Qwen3-235B-A22B decode shapes (odd
block counts, partial workgroups, fused expert weights) and perf cases
for every decode matvec of that model.
